# Host-fetched secrets. `fetch-secrets.sh` writes real credentials into both on
# every container start — see docs/06-devcontainer-setup.md § "The macOS
# Keychain values". The .docker copy is derived from the .env and holds the same
# credentials, so it is listed in its own right rather than left to a glob: a
# glob that later misses a file gives no signal, and two lines make a missing
# one visible.
#
# Adopted, not deployed: hand-written in Phase 0.5 and stamped at register
# contract 18, when `secret_files_are_gitignored` made SEC-001 read these two
# lines instead of a comment claiming it depended on them. One stamp per region
# rather than one at the top — the rest of this file is build output and editor
# droppings that belong to no control, and a whole-file stamp would claim them.
# ee-control: SEC-001  ee-skill: gate-secrets@0.1.0  register: v0.18.0  register-contract: 18
.devcontainer/.env
.devcontainer/.env.docker

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Node
node_modules/

# Editors and OS
.DS_Store

# Local folders to be ignored
temp/
